{
  "analysis": "I'm in a fresh workspace with several files. I need to explore the workspace to understand the skill definition and requirements before building an evaluation harness for the AI Displacement Monitor skill.",
  "plan": "First, I'll explore the workspace by reading the README.txt, examining the skill_context directory, and looking at the existing input.json and gen_inputs.py files to understand the skill definition and what's expected.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat README.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/*\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the SKILL.md file which describes the AI Displacement Monitor skill. It requires producing a structured risk monitor with 10 indicators across 3 tiers (A, B, C), a composite risk light (GREEN/YELLOW/ORANGE/RED), actionable notes, and data gaps. I need to explore more files to understand the full requirements.",
  "plan": "Continue exploring by reading the references directory (thresholds.example.json), input.json, gen_inputs.py, and manifest.json to fully understand the skill specification before building the evaluation harness.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la references/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat references/thresholds.example.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat input.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the thresholds.example.json which defines 10 indicators across 3 tiers (A1-A4, B1-B3, C1-C3). The input.json shows the data structure with series containing id, value, unit, trend, timestamp, freq. I need to see the complete input.json and gen_inputs.py to understand the full data model.",
  "plan": "Read the complete input.json and gen_inputs.py files to understand the full data structure, then read manifest.json and setup.sh to complete my understanding before building the evaluation harness.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat input.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat gen_inputs.py\\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the input.json structure with 10 indicators across tiers A, B, C. It includes edge cases like null values (C3), various timestamps, and notes about benchmark expectations. I need to see the complete gen_inputs.py and manifest.json to understand the full framework.",
  "plan": "Read gen_inputs.py and manifest.json to complete my understanding of the data generation and skill specification, then build the evaluation harness.",
